    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15228#discussion_r4603435254\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Same thing here</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 641319624,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794937831
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15228#discussion_r4603433580\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Can we name this <code>ty_</code> instead, so that we don't in the future accidentally introduce dead code that doesn't get warned about being dead code due to the leading underscore? We've been slowly switching existing <code>_</code>-prefixes to suffixes due to this issue (which we didn't think of when we originally introduced all of these).</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 641319625,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794937831
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15228#discussion_r4603522142\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think we probably also want to have these methods:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pub fn to_rooted(&amp;self, store: impl AsContextMut) -&gt; Rooted&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n<li><code>pub fn ensure_rooted(&amp;mut self, store: impl AsContextMut)</code></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 641319626,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794937831
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15228#discussion_r4603479901\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Should these become <code>.to_rooted(store)</code> or something for future compat so we don't accidentally get panics when introducing unrooted references? (I haven't looked at the next PR yet)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 641319627,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794937832
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15228#discussion_r4603536245\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>And then on <code>Val</code> and <code>Ref</code>, we probably also want</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>pub fn to_rooted(&amp;self, store: impl AsContextMut) -&gt; Self</code></li>\n<li><code>pub fn ensure_rooted(&amp;mut self, store: impl AsContextMut)</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>as well</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 641319628,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794937832
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15228#discussion_r4603489064\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(And similar for ~all the other <code>unwrap_rooted()</code> calls in this PR)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 641319629,
